WEBVTT

00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:15,630
In your opinion, do you think my MRI findings show that I should do something more drastic

00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:17,630
like radiation?

00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:20,710
Would you need to see the actual images to make that opinion?

00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:25,110
And if so, should I get the images to you?

00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:26,110
Thank you.

00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:31,270
So this is a person who showed metastasis to the bone.

00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:38,750
And so the real question is, when would I recommend radiation or at least looking into doing

00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:41,550
radiation when you have metastasis to bone?

00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:49,110
And the answer would be, when you have one or two or three sites where there's a lot

00:00:49,110 --> 00:00:56,510
of damage where there could be pathological fracture, or you have a lot of pain that

00:00:56,510 --> 00:00:58,870
is coming from that site.

00:00:58,870 --> 00:01:13,270
If you have a speckled, which is a radiographic term, if you have a speckled distribution of

00:01:13,270 --> 00:01:22,270
lytic lesions, which radiographically they would say that there's just a broad band speckled

00:01:22,270 --> 00:01:26,630
distribution of lesions throughout the spine or something like that that makes some kind

00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:27,630
of comment like that.

00:01:27,630 --> 00:01:30,150
No radiation really isn't in the order.

00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:39,390
So radiation is something you would do if you had destruction of the L5 vertebrae, the fifth

00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:50,710
lumbar vertebrae or where there's it's concentrated and there's in one or two spots and it's a weight

00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:58,230
buried bone and or it is causing the person a lot of pain.

00:01:58,230 --> 00:02:01,470
So radiation can be beneficial there.

00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:07,830
When it's throughout the whole spine and the person doesn't have specific pain in any areas

00:02:07,830 --> 00:02:13,750
of the spine, maybe they just have generalized fatigue or aching or something like that in the

00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:18,430
spine, then radiation probably would not even be offered by the radiologist.

00:02:18,430 --> 00:02:27,030
So that's, I think that helps answer the question, if that doesn't just feel free to ask more

